# construction calls torch.randn(rank>8 shape, device=gcu) therefore dies
# before flag_gems code even runs -- e.g. tests/test_argwhere.py's 9-D
# edge-shape case, which exercises this op's shape-tensor fallback path.
# High-rank device tensors themselves are fully supported (allocation,
# H2D/D2H transfer and the Triton kernels below all work); only the
# topsaten random/fill kernels are rank-limited. So create the values on
# the host and transfer, preserving torch.randn semantics. Composes with
# add.py's _complex_safe_randn (innermost), linalg_matrix_exp.py's
# _int_safe_randn and quantized_lstm.py's _cuda_redirect_randn. Drop once
# topsaten validates rank instead of terminating.
